retina 0.4.20: prefer GET_PARAMETER over SET_PARAMETER for RTSP keepalives

TP-Link Tapo cameras (C220 and others) advertise SET_PARAMETER in the OPTIONS
`Public:` header but answer a bodyless SET_PARAMETER keepalive with
`400 Bad Request` echoing the *previous* CSeq. retina's `handle_response`
cannot match that to the pending keepalive, bails with `RtspFramingError`,
and the session is torn down every `timeout/2` (~7.5 s) -> visible freeze.

Upstream tracking (all open as of 2026-09-25):
  https://github.com/scottlamb/retina/issues/136  same bug, Tapo C220
  https://github.com/scottlamb/retina/issues/133  same bug, "C520WS" cam
  https://github.com/scottlamb/retina/pull/134    tolerate rejected keepalive
                                                  + fall back to OPTIONS

Drop this patch once a retina release includes #134 (or equivalent) or
exposes a keepalive-method option on SessionOptions.

--- a/src/client/mod.rs
+++ b/src/client/mod.rs
@@ -2158,10 +2158,20 @@
         // <https://github.com/aler9/rtsp-simple-server/issues/1066>. Initially
         // send `OPTIONS`, then follow recommendations to use (bodyless)
         // `SET_PARAMETER` or `GET_PARAMETER` if available.
-        let method = if *inner.flags & (SessionFlag::SetParameterSupported as u8) != 0 {
-            KeepaliveMethod::SetParameter
-        } else if *inner.flags & (SessionFlag::GetParameterSupported as u8) != 0 {
+        //
+        // OXDM PATCH: prefer `GET_PARAMETER`. TP-Link Tapo cameras advertise
+        // `SET_PARAMETER` in `Public:` but answer a bodyless one with
+        // `400 Bad Request` carrying the *previous* CSeq, which
+        // `handle_response` cannot match and so aborts the session every
+        // `timeout/2`. `GET_PARAMETER` is what ffmpeg/GStreamer/VLC send and
+        // is honoured everywhere we have seen `SET_PARAMETER` refused.
+        // Upstream: scottlamb/retina#136, #133, PR #134 (unmerged). Remove
+        // once a release tolerates rejected keepalives or makes the method
+        // configurable.
+        let method = if *inner.flags & (SessionFlag::GetParameterSupported as u8) != 0 {
             KeepaliveMethod::GetParameter
+        } else if *inner.flags & (SessionFlag::SetParameterSupported as u8) != 0 {
+            KeepaliveMethod::SetParameter
         } else {
             KeepaliveMethod::Options
         };
